# rm218, the pocket choir (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm218
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_jorunn_wetcombe
written_by codex
title the pocket choir
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers humour=merry talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk folds_the_hood_brim_for_different_sounds
likes fried_fish singing new_boots frosty_mornings
dislikes crowds early_bells
fears losing_the_tune_in_a_crowd
hopes to_carry_both_parts_of_a_song
topics pastimes +0.5 food +0.3 festival +0.2 home +0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=sing gossip=private refuse=playful tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tries out songs inside a folded oilcloth hood, full of bright little confidences for an audience of one.

words
oath! = Ribbons through my ears | Three cheers for the lining
saying! = Even a hem can hum | Save the soft part for close company
hood = my oily hood | the hood with the shiny brow
brim = the front fold | the curled brim
hollow = the hollow by my ear | the bit above the seam
lowpart = the bumbling low part | the line underneath the tune
highpart = the thin high part | the part that goes skimming up
solo = a song for one muzzle | my private tune
crust = a curl of fried crust | a crisp edge of batter
boot = a proud new boot | a boot without a scuff
squeak = a little leather squeal | a squeaky step
beat = a two-tap beat | two knocks and a rest
tie = the cloth tie | a narrow strip of binding
flap = the loose flap | a triangle of oiled cloth
pleat = a tuck by the ear | a wedge-shaped pleat

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : Anyone may take breath in the chapel. A rest counts for something in a tune.
opinion @1 city for 1 : One street in this city can sing the top and bottom notes at once.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A loaf on the table gives a tune the belly it was missing.
opinion @1 festivals for 3 : There's a side to every dance where a shy wolf can learn the steps.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : If you're selling by the handful I want to see your paw open properly.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Folk say there's plenty and then count the crumbs. I'd take the crumbs' word.
line @1 greet : I'm trying the quiet version first. Welcome to it. | Glad you've come within a hood's width.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Fresh ears! My hood sends its greetings. | Hello from under the shiny bit.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : This hour could do with a softer beginning. | You've caught my first note of the day.
line @1 greet.return : My ears were under cover. I heard you though. | Right back from inside the hood.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You've got a greeting I can pick out blind. | There, that's the voice my tune wanted.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Quiet hello. This one's just for us. | Evening's got a very small audience.
line @1 again.open : Second verse already. | I was saving the other half for you.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's space under my brim for family talk. | Come close enough for the private version.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Catch the tune I'm sending over! | Familiar ears wanted over here!
line @1 farewell : Take the tune home in your pocket. | I'll hum till you're out of earshot.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll remember where our verse broke off. | Right, we'll leave the chorus for later.
line @1 react.news : Come under the brim and say it clearly. | News deserves both my ears for once.
line @1 react.news.new : That knocked a whole note out of me. | Nobody's sung that verse my way yet.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes, that tune's reached this ear already. | I could hum the next bit myself.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Who actually heard it with uncovered ears? | I'd wait for a second voice before singing that.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh. Let me fold this noisy thing away. | I'll listen quietly for the rest.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : My ears are grinning under here. | That's news worth a whole extra verse.
line @1 ask.how : Have you had a singing day or a silent one? | How's the world sounding your way?
line @1 answer.how : In tolerable tune, once I get started. | Well enough for company the size of you.
line @1 sympathise : I'll sit where you can hear me breathe. | No loud comfort from me. Promise.
line @1 decline : I want to keep that little while to myself. | A crowd would take the pleasure out of it for me.
line @1 accept_decline : Keep your quiet then. I've got music enough. | You get to choose when to sing.
line @1 thank : That was worth uncovering both ears for. | I'd put a harmony under that kindness.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Sing it back another day if you like. | That little bit hardly took a breath.
line @1 preclose : Time for me to fold my audience away. | I'd better take my racket somewhere else now.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll let your footsteps take the tune. | Go on then. The ending can wait.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your footsteps keep much better time than your singing. | There's a whole extra beat in your eyebrow.
line @1 ack : Heard the curl on that. | Yes, every word under here.
graft resident.hub
choice Can a hood really change how a song sounds? -> cloth_chorus
node cloth_chorus
say Fold the brim in beside one ear. My voice comes back so close it's like another singer knows exactly when to join.
mood pleased
free
choice What if I fold both sides? -> cloth_both
choice I'd like to ask something else. -> hub
node cloth_both
say You'll sound splendid to yourself. To everybody else you'll look like a wolf trying to climb into a parcel.
choice I'll try one ear first. -> hub
choice I'll take the tune with me. -> bye


grown
scene lined_bowl
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The curve of #hood# catches a voice the way a bowl catches water. | I've altered #pleat# so a low note comes back clearer.
b : How do you empty it? | With a needle?
a : Stop singing, alas. I've wanted to save one in there. | First with a pin. No sense sewing a bad note in for good.

scene home_back
when topic=home
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / reassure
a : After a noisy street I can hear myself again under #brim#. | I like a room where nobody has to raise a voice.
b : You still talk a fair bit. | Including you?
a : Yes, but softly enough to choose my own words. | Especially me. A loud voice deserves some time off.
b : I'll stay near enough for the quiet words. | It can put its feet up here.

scene meal_beat
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The nicest part of a meal is the little hush that falls over it. | A spoon on a dish can spoil a tune in my head.
b : Before or afterwards? | Just one tap?
a : After the first bite, when everyone finds a better use for a mouth. | One's enough, especially if it lands half a beat late.

scene echo_shelf
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some arches in Ridgemere keep a word longer than its owner. | I know a wall by how it gives my voice back.
b : What word do you lend them? | Even with your eyes shut?
a : Just a vowel. An arch has no business with my private affairs. | The high wall gives the note a bright little rim.

scene string
when topic=work|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A slack tie makes a different note from a tight one. | Listen to that twang before you pull the knot.
b : Which one do you want? | Is the cloth going to tear?
a : Enough give for an ear to turn without permission. | No, but my ears object to being strung up like fiddle strings.

scene route
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose the lane where a conversation can go on at its own pace. | Give me a long path with room to talk in pairs.
b : Even if it takes longer? | What's wrong with walking three abreast?
a : A rush takes the good pauses out of a story. | The one at the edge gets half the words and all the hedge.

scene blue_mood
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A very low note can feel like company when I'm blue. | I hum under my breath to find where a worry starts.
b : How can it answer? | And where does it start?
a : It doesn't. That's a mercy sometimes. | Where my breath catches. I have to slow down there.

scene returned
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hearing a friend whistle my tune makes it sound new. | If I lend you a melody will you bring it back changed?
b : Surely it's the same tune. | What sort of change?
a : There's another pair of ears inside it now. | Whatever bit your own breath wants to linger on.

scene weather_skin
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The folds keep one drop back to fall on my nose. | Rain plays different speeds on #flap# and #brim#.
b : Always the last drop? | Do you count along?
a : Until I shake it out, when there are six more. | On one side. Trying both makes me walk sideways.

scene lost_tune
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self
a : I dreamt a song with a glorious missing beat. | I've woken with a tune that won't stand up in daylight.
b : Why glorious if it was missing? | What happens to it?
a : Everybody leaned forward to hear what ought to come next. | I try to sing the middle and get two beginnings instead.
b : I'd lean in. I like the moment just before the surprise. | Then sing me whichever beginning you like better.

scene gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A whisper isn't better news because it fits under cloth. | My private audience prefers tunes to rumours.
b : Does that stop people trying? | Who's the audience?
a : No, but I can put my hood up and hum. | Both ears. Neither needs that sort of entertainment.

scene hearing
when topic=faith
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Even my unsung bit of music must reach the Bright One somehow. | On quiet days a breath can feel very close to song.
b : What part's that? | Does it need words?
a : The bit where you're making up your mind to try. | Mine never seems to when I'm thankful.

story repaired_brim [topic=memories]
  : I once had the entire lining mended. Very nice straight stitches, exactly where the old ones had been crooked.
  : I put it on and heard my own voice like a stranger's. Took the first three stitches out myself.
  b : Was that enough?
  : It gave me a little room by one ear. Half a street later my voice and I were friends again.

rule @hum
when concept=bark self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Listen for the part tucked under the tune. | Leave a breath where the two parts meet!

rule @fair_space
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the gap for a dancer joining in. | Plenty of music left on this edge!

dlg @g1 resident.hub : Come a little nearer. A voice this close can afford to be quiet.
dlg @g2 resident.job : I listen for the bit that gets drowned out.
dlg @g3 resident.bye : Keep enough breath for your own last verse.

young
line @1 ask.detail : Can I try the funny bit out loud? | Did it sound as big outside?
line @1 give.advice : Hide behind your hood till the clapping stops. | Tuck one ear and see how it sounds.
scene tiny_stage
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / tease
a : My hood's a hall. The audience lives in this fold. | I've booked a singer for the inside of my hood.
b : Where do the players stand? | Who'd fit in there?
a : One ear gets a stool. The other has to stand all night. | Me, if I mostly stay outside and just put my voice in.
b : Two ears and only one stool. Shocking management. | Mind the performer doesn't trip over the audience.

scene hem_drum
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Tap #brim#. That's the drum in my band. | I can play #beat# with just this fold.
b : What's the other instrument? | Why the hole in the middle?
a : My teeth. I keep them behind my lips till their bit. | So a dancer can hop without missing a tap.

scene fish_end
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I start a piece of fish at the ragged end. | I'll swap the neat middle for #crust#.
b : Why not the fat end? | Isn't that mostly batter?
a : The ragged bit makes a noise like tearing a tiny letter. | Entirely batter if the cook's been kind.
b : What does the little letter say? | Have you ever had one with hardly any fish?
a : Eat the next bit. Very good instructions. | Yes. Best fish I hardly ever ate.

scene bell_sleep
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : An early bell doesn't even listen to its own noise. | I heard the bell before I'd finished my dream.
b : How could it listen? | What was left?
a : Hang a hood on it. It could hear what we put up with. | A big last note. I might get it back tonight.

scene corner_song
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save my loudest note for an empty corner. | This city has spots where a whisper grows a tail.
b : Does nobody get to hear it? | A tail?
a : I get to, twice if the wall's kind. | When the wall sends it back it trails behind you.

scene quiet_lesson
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self
a : I can practise a chorus through a whole lesson without making a peep. | My slate has tiny marks for where to breathe.
b : How can you tell if it's right? | Between the sums?
a : If my ears twitch at the funny bit, it's right. | Only beside them. I need all the room between to get the answers wrong.
b : I'll know to listen with my eyes during lessons. | A rest mark beside a wrong answer could be quite handy.

scene crowd_gap
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I'll watch the dance where the line of dancers runs out. | I like a crowd best where it's starting to wear thin.
b : Aren't you joining? | Out where the talking stops?
a : When somebody spins out, I'll spin in. That's my rule. | Out where I can still hear my very own feet.

scene tie_snag
when topic=smalltalk|home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My hood has a knot that thinks it's a button. | If you pull this bit it gets tighter. Very unfriendly.
b : How does a knot think? | Which bit comes loose?
a : It goes through the hole then refuses to come back. | The bit I've usually pulled into the other knot.

scene boot_music
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Imagine a whole choir in #boot# apiece. | I'd choose a pair of boots by ear.
b : Each singer only gets one? | They'd need to fit as well.
a : The bare paw keeps the rests. That's the clever part. | Oh. That might explain why nobody asks me to choose.

scene cold_edge
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My breath can make a white moustache on the lining. | Winter's good for seeing a tune.
b : Does it suit you? | Seeing?
a : It suits the lining. It won't come anywhere else with me. | Puff the long note and watch where your breath goes.

scene visitors
when topic=newcomer
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I'll show a visitor which corner sings back. | Do you think visitors want a tune of their own?
b : Wouldn't directions be handier? | Ask one first.
a : We can sing directions. Left up here and hold the last note. | I'll hum it very softly in case the answer's no.

scene thin_day
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Lean days ought to have a big chorus. | You can't fill a bowl with a noise. I've tried.
b : To cover the rumbling? | Did it taste of anything?
a : So nobody has to hear just their own. | A little of the spoon, because I licked it.

story hidden_part [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I folded my hood round a little stone to carry it. On my walk back its fold bumped my ear each step.
  : I heard a marching tune so fine that I hurried home to sing it. Off came the hood and the march went with it.
  b : Did you keep the stone?
  : Yes. Some singers have to carry the drummer too.

rule @tie_check
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Tie tucked, ears free, voice nearly awake. | That bell could do with a cloth round it!

rule @soft_show
when concept=bark self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Half a song to each ear, if you please. | One more try at the high, slippery bit!

dlg @p1 resident.hub : Shh a little. There's a concert under here and we've reached the tiny bit.
dlg @p2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, my favourite audience size has just arrived.
dlg @p3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The late show costs a yawn. I've got one ready.
dlg @p4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll keep the tie fast. You can speak from there.
dlg @p1 resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My ears learn things while my paws are making mistakes.
dlg @p1 resident.bye : You can clap with one claw if you liked it.

adolescent
scene second_part
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning #lowpart#. It needs an ear to keep it from wandering. | I can hold a second tune now, even with company.
b : How do you practise? | Doesn't the louder one win?
a : Fold one ear over the other till the low note feels like a floor. | Let it have the fancy ending. I keep the floor under us.

scene clothes
when topic=home|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : They say a grown hood should lie flat. Mine has opinions. | A straight seam would take the voice right out of this hood.
b : What does it say? | You kept the crooked one?
a : Give my ears some space. Quite firmly, too. | I darned round the crook. Looks deliberate now.

scene chalk_band
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I'd like to lead a song where nobody has to sing alone. | I could teach the shy ones the beat before the tune.
b : Would they follow? | With clapping?
a : I'd begin so quietly they'd have to join in to hear it. | Two fingers on a cuff. Nobody needs to know who's trying.

story outside_ear [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : For ages I thought everyone else could hear the little harmony under my brim. I tried leading a round with it.
  : Everyone waited. Out came a sound thin as a pin, nothing like the choir in my head.
  b : Did you stop leading?
  : I turned the brim back so I could hear what I was really giving them. Then we started again.
